      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What makes MEMS and sensor assembly different?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The sensing element must continue interacting with its environment after assembly. This requires low-stress die attach and package structures that protect the device while maintaining pressure, optical, gas or other required access.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What packaging types do you offer?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana supports cavity and open-cavity packages, media-access / ported packages, and selective gel or glob-top protection.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How do you protect sensor accuracy?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Low-stress die attach and stress-decoupling adhesives help limit mechanical loading on the sensing element. The process is developed and qualified during first-article builds.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality systems apply?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
